assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

T1  byte fidelity end to end: what repl_step sent is what repl_text
    returns — through the args encoding INBOUND and the yxml
    stripping OUTBOUND (I4). risk to check: XML.content on the result
    must not eat Isabelle symbols like \<Longrightarrow> or collapse
    whitespace inside string literals.
    test [ml unit]: step a lemma containing \<Longrightarrow>, an
    inner string with two spaces, and an embedded newline; text
    output equals the concatenation verbatim.
    test [bridge]: the same through session.ir — asserts the scala
    stripping side.
T2  zero steps -> ok with empty output (not an error); the model
    probes freely.
    test [ml unit]: init, text -> ok, empty.
T3  full chain: extract-and-splice.
    test [e2e]: prove a lemma over two steps, repl_text, write the
    text into a .thy fixture, load_theory checks it (spec workflow
    steps 5-7; shares the fixture with plans/check_theory).

